# NEARS-3842 fix-cycle-1 bug: flag ON + mixed basket + no active module -> tapping "+" on ANY cart row flips the active module to cartList[0]'s module AND the increment is lost (1->2->1)
# device emulator-5570, build 130cd1d0d (feat/NEARS-3842-cart-per-store-groups), backend worktree :8242 on private copy nears_qa_3842 (flag=1)
# mechanism: cart_item_widget.dart onIncrement (~:723) calls cartController.forcefullySetModule(cartList[0].item!.moduleId!) BEFORE the step.
#   forcefullySetModule acts only when ModuleController.module == null (cart_service.dart:67) -> setModule(cartList[0] module) + HomeController.loadData(true)
#   -> home reload re-GETs customer/cart/list, which lands BEFORE the increment's cart/update completes -> a second cart/update POST writes the stale quantity back.
#   Before NEARS-3842, cart initCall always auto-selected cartList[0]'s module, so module was never null in the cart and this call was a no-op. AC5 now (correctly) leaves it null.
